        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Economics and Game Theory - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "2. **Mechanism design = systems design for rational agents:** When agents have private information and self-interested behavior, how do you design a system that still achieves good outcomes? This is exactly what distributed systems engineers face when incentives matter."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
